    },
    "middle": {
      "text": "Stuck-in-the-middle: neither identity bought, both costs paid."
    }
  },
  "why": "A cost leader's mix is not 'the same marketing, done cheaper' — the position and the mix stand or fall together."
};

const scTradeoffSpot = {
  "prompt": "One line of this Southwest trade-off summary is wrong. Find it.",
  "lines": [
    "Southwest runs point-to-point, no meals, no assigned seats, one aircraft type",
    "A full-service rival could copy any single choice tomorrow",
    "Copying the whole system strands the rival's own hubs, crews and frequent-flyer machine",
    "So the rival copies the system and keeps its own position intact",
    "Strategy is the set of things you deliberately refuse to do"
  ],
  "errorLine": 3,
  "correction": "So the rival must abandon its own position to copy — imitation is self-destructive, which is what defends the position.",
  "why": "A position is defensible only as a system of trade-offs: without them nothing stops an equal rival from doing exactly what you do, and the profit is borrowed, not owned."
};

