  <p>
    <strong>What to notice:</strong> the three questions replay the lesson's spine — structure
    beats effort (buyer power caps identical products differently), precision has a price
    (the 1/√n rule at 400 respondents gives a margin of about 5 points), and coherence is the
    trap (a bolted-on no-frills system delivers the costs of neither model). Each wrong
    answer is the mistake the framework exists to prevent.
  </p>
